311
00:22:52.679 --> 00:22:56.720
application. You put your card in and pay everything

312
00:22:56.720 --> 00:22:58.589
you want to pay here.

313
00:23:01.279 --> 00:23:03.120
Look, do you see up there?

314
00:23:03.120 --> 00:23:08.630
This is what ePay.bg looks like. It's an app, you log in,

315
00:23:09.080 --> 00:23:13.200
register a card, register your bills, and once you've

316
00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:17.709
paid them, they will show up every time you have a new

317
00:23:18.679 --> 00:23:21.550
bill, and you can pay them through Viber as well.

318
00:23:22.640 --> 00:23:25.480
Online is best. In Italy I don't know if we have a cash desk.

319
00:23:25.480 --> 00:23:30.950
Maybe not. Anyone

320
00:23:34.960 --> 00:23:37.109
else, or shall I ask the last one.

321
00:23:38.240 --> 00:23:44.240
What was the biggest mistake or lesson you learned

322
00:23:44.240 --> 00:23:48.720
when entering foreign markets that, had you known it earlier,

323
00:23:48.720 --> 00:23:54.030
would have saved you a lot of headaches and effort?

324
00:23:59.679 --> 00:24:01.120
That's an interesting question.

325
00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:06.360
Honestly, I would say the biggest lesson

326
00:24:06.360 --> 00:24:09.880
I wish I had known in advance was whether Trump would attack

327
00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:14.960
Iran, because of the projects we had in the Middle East,

328
00:24:14.960 --> 00:24:16.310
since it had an impact.

329
00:24:17.120 --> 00:24:21.440
What I would say a bit more generally, of course,

330
00:24:21.440 --> 00:24:27.679
is specifically to not lose your DNA when you start.

331
00:24:27.679 --> 00:24:31.750
As a small company that is developing right now,

332
00:24:32.399 --> 00:24:35.559
I very often have to change my business model

333
00:24:35.559 --> 00:24:39.960
to adapt to the market, which requires analysis,

334
00:24:39.960 --> 00:24:43.840
quick decisions, but sometimes a blurring of focus.

335
00:24:43.840 --> 00:24:47.799
At least that was the case in the first year, and for me what

336
00:24:47.799 --> 00:24:51.360
I wished would not happen is that very

337
00:24:51.360 --> 00:24:54.080
blurring. But maybe those are the baby steps

338
00:24:54.080 --> 00:24:57.109
you had to go through to reach the next stage.

339
00:24:58.360 --> 00:25:05.480
That's it. We haven't had dramas, but we haven't had

340
00:25:05.480 --> 00:25:08.320
such abrupt entries into markets.

341
00:25:08.320 --> 00:25:12.070
In general, we have tried to do it slowly,

342
00:25:12.480 --> 00:25:17.960
without giant investments, so that if something fails, there are no

343
00:25:17.960 --> 00:25:22.829
big consequences. So this is rather the principle:

344
00:25:23.799 --> 00:25:25.349
slowly, deliberately,

345
00:25:26.360 --> 00:25:31.279
often, almost always with partners, and so far we have

346
00:25:31.279 --> 00:25:35.750
rarely made mistakes that cost us a lot of money.

347
00:25:37.440 --> 00:25:43.720
Thank you very much, Lora, Niki, for this conversation,

